    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "🔁 1. Switch Your Internet Connection",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Temporarily switch from Wi-Fi/LAN to your mobile data. If the website loads, the issue is with your local network. You can switch back after verifying.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "🌐 2. Restart Your Router or Modem",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Power cycle your network device to clear up temporary glitches.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "🌍 3. Try a Different Browser or Device",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "This helps determine if the issue is specific to your browser or device.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "🧼 4. Reset Your Browser Settings",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Sometimes, extensions, cookies, or incorrect settings can cause trouble.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "In Chrome: Settings > Reset Settings > Restore settings to their original defaults",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "h2",
     "text": "Advance Fixes",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "24px",
     "color": "rgb(250, 232, 238)",
     "anchor": "advance-fixes"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "🔧 Option 1: Restart DNS Client (Windows)",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Press Windows + R → type services.msc",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "In the Services list, find DNS Client",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Right-click → Click Restart",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Reopen your browser and test the website.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "🍎 Option 1: Flush DNS Settings (Mac)",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Open System Preferences → Go to Network",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Choose your connection → Click Advanced",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Open the DNS tab → Select and remove any custom DNS entries using the “–” button",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Click OK → Exit settings",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "🌐 Option 2: Change DNS Servers",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "Sometimes switching to Google Public DNS can resolve delays.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "For Windows and Mac:",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "IPv4: 8.8.8.8 and/or 8.8.4.4",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "IPv6: 2001:4860:4860::8888 and/or 2001:4860:4860::8844",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "h2",
     "text": "Still Not Working?",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "24px",
     "color": "rgb(208, 23, 82)",
     "anchor": "still-not-working"
    },
    {
     "tag": "p",
     "text": "If none of the above steps resolve the issue, consider:",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "The website might be down or under maintenance.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "Your firewall/antivirus might be blocking the connection.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "li",
     "text": "The hosted server could be experiencing downtime.",
     "href": "",
     "src": "",
     "alt": "",
     "size": "16px",
     "color": "rgb(33, 33, 33)"
    },
    {
     "tag": "h3",
     "text": "The \"took too long to respond\" error might be annoying, but it's usually easy to fix. Whether it’s a DNS hiccup, slow internet, or browser glitch, following these steps should help you get back online in no time.",
